			  ADDITIONAL TERMS:
			TRANSPARENCY CLAUSE

In accordance with Section 7 ("Additional Terms") of the GNU AGPLv3, the following additional permissions and restrictions apply:

1. MODIFICATION TRANSPARENCY
It is strictly prohibited to modify the logic of the backend software (API, Consensus, Storage, or Protocol logic) without informing users that the server is running a modified version.

If you modify the Source Code and deploy it as a network service:
    a) You MUST prominently display a "Modified Version" notice in the initial connection handshake or API response headers (e.g., `X-Server-Version: my-fork-v1-modified`).
    b) You MUST provide a mechanism for users to verify the integrity of the running code (e.g., a public link to the source code of your specific modification).
    c) You MUST NOT misrepresent your modified node as a standard/official node of the original protocol.

2. LOGIC INTEGRITY
You may not alter the cryptographic verification logic (signature checking, hash generation) in a way that would allow the server to forge messages on behalf of users or bypass authentication, unless such modification is clearly labeled as a "Unsecured/Test Mode" and is not used for real user data.

FAILURE TO COMPLY WITH THIS TRANSPARENCY CLAUSE TERMINATES YOUR RIGHTS UNDER THIS LICENSE.
